<div class="ed-reading guide-reading text-lg">
<p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-muted">A useful home office does not need to be expensive or perfectly styled. Start with the equipment you already have and observe how you use it during a normal day. Look for avoidable friction: a charger that gets pulled across the desk, a screen that catches glare, a camera that points too low, or a cable that crosses a walking path. Make small, reversible changes and test the setup before buying anything.</p>
<section class="ed-start" id="start" aria-labelledby="start-heading"><p class="ed-label">Start here</p><h2 id="start-heading">Start with the everyday workflow</h2><p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-muted">Map the devices, positions and connections that matter during a normal work session.</p><div class="ed-choices">
